---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CostDesign from '../../../components/CostDesign.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Cost per successful AI task calculator"
  description="Calculate what acceptable AI outcomes cost, including failed attempts, retries, tools, infrastructure, and human review. A free browser-only tool."
>
  <article class="shell page-content cost-page">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <a class="eyebrow back-link" href="/projects/">
        ← The open lab
      </a>
      <h1>
        What does a useful
        <br />
        <span>AI outcome cost?</span>
      </h1>
      <p>
        Put the whole batch in the numerator. Put acceptable outcomes in the
        denominator.
      </p>
      <p class="pill">Illustrative planning tool · No model rankings</p>
    </header>
    <div class="cost-intro prose">
      <p>
        Use totals for one evaluation window. Include{' '}
        <strong>every attempt and retry</strong>, including those that failed.
        Define success before comparing designs; an agent saying “done” is not
        an acceptance check.
      </p>
      <p>
        The starting numbers are <strong>invented examples</strong> from{' '}
        <a href="/notes/cost-of-a-completed-task/">
          The cost of a completed task
        </a>
        . Replace them with your own measurements. All amounts are USD; convert
        other currencies before entering them.
      </p>
    </div>
    <noscript>
      <p class="cost-notice">
        Enable JavaScript to use the interactive calculator. The formula and
        worked example below remain available.
      </p>
    </noscript>
    <form id="cost-form" hidden novalidate autocomplete="off">
      <div class="cost-mode">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" id="compare-designs" /> Compare two designs
        </label>
        <p>
          Use the same attempted tasks, acceptance rule, and cost categories for
          both.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cost-designs">
        <CostDesign design="a" />
        <CostDesign design="b" />
      </div>
      <p id="cost-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
      <div class="cost-actions">
        <button class="button primary" type="submit">
          Calculate outcome cost
        </button>
        <button class="button secondary" type="reset">
          Reset example
        </button>
      </div>
      <p class="cost-privacy">
        Calculated in your browser. Values are not saved, uploaded, or included
        in links; refresh restores the example. Zeros exclude a cost category
        unless your measured cost was actually zero.
      </p>
    </form>
    <section
      id="cost-results"
      class="cost-results"
      aria-labelledby="cost-results-heading"
      tabindex="-1"
      hidden
    >
      <p class="eyebrow">From your inputs</p>
      <h2 id="cost-results-heading">Cost and completion, together.</h2>
      <div class="cost-result-grid"></div>
      <p id="cost-comparison"></p>
      <p class="cost-result-note">
        A lower cost per success does not establish equivalent quality, safety,
        latency, or suitability. Review the acceptance rule and excluded costs.
      </p>
      <button class="button secondary" type="button" id="copy-cost">
        Copy results
      </button>
      <p id="copy-cost-status" role="status"></p>
      <div id="cost-copy-fallback" hidden>
        <label for="cost-summary">Select and copy these results</label>
        <textarea id="cost-summary" readonly rows="12"></textarea>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="prose cost-method">
      <h2 id="method">The method</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Total included cost</strong> = model + tools + infrastructure +
        (review minutes × hourly human cost ÷ 60).
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Cost per successful task</strong> = total included cost ÷
        successful tasks. If no tasks succeed, this value is undefined: report
        “no successful completions.”
      </p>
      <p>
        Use actual batch totals where possible. Review includes remediation and
        verification if you choose to include them. Shared overhead, acquisition
        costs, setup work, and other categories are excluded unless you allocate
        them explicitly. Avoid double-counting costs already bundled in another
        charge.
      </p>
      <h2>A worked example</h2>
      <p>
        Two invented designs attempt the same 100 tasks under the same
        acceptance rule. Human review and infrastructure are excluded.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Metric</th>
            <th>Design A</th>
            <th>Design B</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th>Total cost</th>
            <td>$3.00</td>
            <td>$5.00</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Successful tasks</th>
            <td>40</td>
            <td>90</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Cost per success</th>
            <td>$0.075</td>
            <td>About $0.0556</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        Design A spends less overall; Design B costs less per acceptable result.
        Neither is a universal winner. Use this calculation alongside{' '}
        <a href="/notes/comparing-ai-models/">
          an evaluation of your application's requirements
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <h2>Inspect the assumptions</h2>
      <p>
        This is arithmetic on supplied values, not a price forecast or a
        measured model evaluation. Success rates are inputs. The calculator does
        not assume independent retries or estimate how reliability changes with
        more attempts. Read the{' '}
        <a href="/notes/cost-of-a-completed-task/">source-backed cost guide</a>{' '}
        and inspect{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/swapupg/swapupg.github.io/blob/main/src/lib/task-cost.ts">
          the calculation source
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/swapupg/swapupg.github.io/issues/new?title=Task%20cost%20calculator">
          Suggest a correction or improvement ↗
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
<script>
  import {
    assessTaskCost,
    parseCostValue,
    formatCost,
    type TaskCostInput,
  } from '../../../lib/task-cost';
  const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#cost-form')!;
  const compare = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#compare-designs')!;
  const second =
    document.querySelector<HTMLFieldSetElement>('[data-design="b"]')!;
  const results = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#cost-results')!;
  const error = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#cost-error')!;
  const fallback = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#cost-copy-fallback')!;
  const summary = document.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('#cost-summary')!;
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#copy-cost-status')!;
  let plainSummary = '';
  const hideResults = () => {
    results.hidden = true;
    fallback.hidden = true;
    status.textContent = '';
  };
  const syncComparison = () => {
    second.hidden = !compare.checked;
    second.disabled = !compare.checked;
    hideResults();
  };
  form.hidden = false;
  form.addEventListener('input', hideResults);
  compare.addEventListener('change', syncComparison);
  form.addEventListener('reset', (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    for (const input of form.querySelectorAll('input')) {
      input.value = input.defaultValue;
      input.checked = input.defaultChecked;
    }
    syncComparison();
    error.hidden = true;
  });
  // Browsers can restore form values on reload or history navigation.
  window.addEventListener('pageshow', () => form.reset());
  form.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    hideResults();
    error.hidden = true;
    const grid = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.cost-result-grid')!;
    grid.replaceChildren();
    const evaluated: {
      id: string;
      input: TaskCostInput;
      result: ReturnType<typeof assessTaskCost>;
    }[] = [];
    try {
      for (const id of compare.checked ? ['a', 'b'] : ['a']) {
        const input = {} as TaskCostInput;
        const fields = form.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>(
          `[data-design="${id}"] input`,
        );
        for (const field of fields) {
          if (!field.checkValidity()) {
            field.reportValidity();
            field.focus();
            throw new Error(
              `Design ${id.toUpperCase()}: check ${field.labels?.[0]?.textContent || 'this field'}.`,
            );
          }
          input[field.dataset.costField as keyof TaskCostInput] =
            parseCostValue(field.value);
        }
        evaluated.push({ id, input, result: assessTaskCost(input) });
      }
      if (
        evaluated.length === 2 &&
        evaluated[0].input.attempted !== evaluated[1].input.attempted
      )
        throw new Error(
          'Use the same number of attempted tasks for a comparison.',
        );
      const text: string[] = [
        'Model Fieldnotes — task cost calculation',
        'Inputs supplied by the reader; not a model benchmark. Currency: USD.',
      ];
      for (const { id, input, result } of evaluated) {
        const card = document.createElement('div');
        card.className = 'cost-result-card';
        const heading = document.createElement('h3');
        heading.textContent = `Design ${id.toUpperCase()}`;
        card.append(heading);
        const primary = document.createElement('p');
        primary.className = 'cost-primary';
        primary.textContent =
          result.perSuccess === null
            ? 'No successful completions'
            : formatCost(result.perSuccess);
        card.append(primary);
        const subtitle = document.createElement('p');
        subtitle.textContent = 'Per successful task';
        card.append(subtitle);
        const dl = document.createElement('dl');
        const rows = [
          ['Total included cost', formatCost(result.total)],
          [
            'Completion rate',
            `${(result.completionRate * 100).toFixed(1)}% (${input.succeeded} / ${input.attempted})`,
          ],
          ['Cost per attempted task', formatCost(result.perAttempt)],
          [
            'Model / tools / infrastructure',
            `${formatCost(input.model)} / ${formatCost(input.tools)} / ${formatCost(input.infrastructure)}`,
          ],
          [
            'Human review cost',
            `${formatCost(result.human)} (${input.reviewMinutes} min at ${formatCost(input.hourlyCost)}/hour)`,
          ],
        ];
        for (const [label, value] of rows) {
          const dt = document.createElement('dt');
          dt.textContent = label;
          const dd = document.createElement('dd');
          dd.textContent = value;
          dl.append(dt, dd);
        }
        card.append(dl);
        grid.append(card);
        text.push(
          '',
          `Design ${id.toUpperCase()}: ${primary.textContent} per successful task`,
          ...rows.map(([label, value]) => `${label}: ${value}`),
        );
      }
      document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#cost-comparison')!.textContent =
        compare.checked
          ? 'Compare total spend, completion, and cost per success together. Use the same acceptance criteria for both designs.'
          : '';
      text.push(
        '',
        'Includes only entered costs across the full batch, including failures and retries. Check exclusions and acceptance criteria.',
        'https://modelfieldnotes.com/tools/task-cost/',
      );
      plainSummary = text.join('\n');
      results.hidden = false;
      results.focus();
    } catch (err) {
      error.textContent =
        err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Check your inputs and try again.';
      error.hidden = false;
    }
  });
  document.querySelector('#copy-cost')!.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(plainSummary);
      status.textContent = 'Results copied.';
    } catch {
      summary.value = plainSummary;
      fallback.hidden = false;
      summary.focus();
      summary.select();
      status.textContent =
        'Copy is unavailable. Select and copy the results below.';
    }
  });
</script>
